# Trivy findings accepted for the ModerServer platform.
# Every entry needs a reason; CVE entries also need an expiry date so they are
# re-evaluated instead of being ignored forever.

# --- Kubernetes RBAC checks (static chart scans) ---------------------------
# These fire on controllers whose job requires the flagged permission.

# KSV-0041: role can manage Secrets.
# cert-manager stores issued certificates and keys in Secrets; Argo CD and the
# gateway controller read and write the Secrets of the resources they manage.
KSV-0041

# KSV-0044: role with wildcard verbs on wildcard resources.
# The Argo CD application controller applies arbitrary manifests from Git and
# is cluster-admin by design.
KSV-0044

# KSV-0046: role can manage all resources.
# Same Argo CD application controller ClusterRole as KSV-0044.
KSV-0046

# KSV-0114: role can manage admission webhook configurations.
# The cert-manager CA injector writes the CA bundle into webhook configurations.
KSV-0114

# KSV-0056: role can manage Services.
# The gateway controller creates the Service of the NGINX data plane it
# provisions. The permission is a namespaced Role limited to nginx-gateway.
KSV-0056

# --- Vulnerabilities in upstream binaries -----------------------------------
# ModerServer repackages the upstream cert-manager v1.21.3 binaries; these are
# fixed by a cert-manager release that bumps the dependency, not by this repo.

# golang.org/x/net v0.60.0 (fixed in v0.62.0) in the cert-manager binaries
CVE-2026-78661 exp:2027-02-15

# github.com/go-jose/go-jose/v4 v4.1.4 (fixed in v4.1.6) in cert-manager-controller
CVE-2026-116587 exp:2027-02-15
